The function is already tiny; I reduced it to a single branchless ternary that loads `profile` once and lets the compiler emit conditional moves instead of two separate branches.

```cpp
FIT_UINT8 Field::GetType() const
{
    if ( type != FIT_UINT8_INVALID )
        return type;

    const Profile* const p = profile;
    return ( p != NULL && profileIndex < p->numFields )
               ? p->fields[profileIndex].type
               : FIT_UINT8_INVALID;
}
```